  "title": "AlloyDB Read Pool Autoscaling Arrives",
  "summary": "AlloyDB now supports autoscaling for read pools, allowing you to dynamically adjust the number of read replica nodes based on CPU utilization or predefined schedules. This significantly simplifies managing read capacity and optimizing costs.",
  "details": "A major new capability has landed: AlloyDB read pools can now be configured for autoscaling. The `ReadPoolConfig` schema gains a new `autoScalingConfig` property, which references the newly introduced `AutoScalingConfig` schema. This configuration allows you to define an autoscaling `Policy`, including `maxNodeCount` and `coolDownPeriodSec`, and specify `CpuUtilization` targets. Furthermore, you can set up detailed `schedules` using the new `Schedule` schema, enabling cron-based scaling adjustments with properties like `minNodeCount`, `durationSec`, and `timeZone`. This feature provides powerful tools for managing your AlloyDB read workloads efficiently.",
